Execution brief from the accepted critical path. Consume TASK-260715-1juybj_contract.md sections 6 and 10 for atomic non-waiting reservations, admission ordering, SOCKS failure mapping, accounting equations, finite terminal reasons, and privacy exclusions. Consume accepted TASK-260715-1i49fm diagnostics APIs and schemas; extend them without destination, hostname, address, port, payload, credential, or high-cardinality labels. Compose cleanly with TASK-260715-sdnk2k bounded pump but do not implement downstream terminal lifecycle TASK-260715-1n9v9o. Preserve the goal invariant that final flow, opening, and byte ceilings remain injectable evidence gates: validate policy and prove bounded behavior, but do not hardcode final physical-tuning values. No SSH-engine selection or engine-specific imports. Exercise below, at, and above all independent limits, concurrent reserve/release races, every terminal cleanup path, fairness of already-admitted flows, deterministic immediate rejects with no side queue or SSH open, diagnostics generation reset, and return to exact baseline under churn. Run focused tests, TSan for concurrent accounting, full core validation, strict format, boundary/privacy guards, and task-board validation. Record exact commands and measured evidence in a task-scoped outcome resource; stop only for an evidence-backed platform or architecture conflict, never a workaround.


