codex
The prior review is reproducible from the code: current gauges are queued as independent updates, and reservation IDs wrap with `&+=`. I’m replacing those two mechanisms with a generation-scoped lock-free absolute-gauge reconciler and a non-reusing exhaustible ID sequence, then I’ll add the requested race, overflow, deinit, stale-generation, and sustained-pressure tests. The skill’s stop-the-line rule does not trigger here—the accepted architecture supports both changes cleanly.
