LOGBOOK.md:11:- DIAGNOSTICS: Runtime schema v1 is additively extended to 138 fixed counters, 75 fixed gauges, and two 12-bucket cumulative histograms. The TCP surface contains only aggregate pressure/terminal tokens, counts, bytes, health, and channel-open latency; it accepts no destination, hostname, address, port, payload, credential, flow/channel ID, or free-form label. Maximum populated encoding is 13,499 bytes of the 65,536-byte limit and generation advancement resets all TCP state.
LOGBOOK.md:12:- VERIFICATION: Eight admission tests cover below/at/above every independent ceiling, 128/256-way concurrent reserve races, SOCKS/SSH fail-fast behavior, admitted-flow fairness, every terminal reason across 320 churn lifecycles, late-open cleanup, exact baseline return, diagnostics reset, and privacy. Focused normal and TSan admission/diagnostics suites pass; `make validate-core` passes boundary/native gates, 296 tests in 27 suites, and the post-test build; strict recursive Swift format, diff, and board validation pass.
LOGBOOK.md:18:- VERIFICATION: Focused normal and Thread Sanitizer suites pass 12 tests, twenty repeated seeded runs pass, strict recursive Swift format passes, and the second `make validate-core` passes 288 tests in 26 suites plus build. The first full run exposed one unrelated existing concurrent provider-failure assertion (`iOS` expected 1007, observed 1009); its isolated rerun and the full rerun passed without pump changes.
LOGBOOK.md:36:- VERIFICATION: Focused normal and Thread Sanitizer runs each pass 58 tests in 2 suites; `make validate-core` passes 276 tests in 25 suites plus build; strict Swift format, diff, and board checks pass; sequential iOS Simulator and universal macOS adapter builds succeed.
LOGBOOK.md:107:- IMPLEMENTATION: `TunnelRuntimeCoordinator` owns one actor-serialized generation and a tracked startup task. It retains each successful acquisition before the next cancellation check, rejects repeat starts, discards mismatched-generation health events, and coalesces caller cancellation, provider stop, startup failure, and mandatory health loss through one shielded cleanup task.
LOGBOOK.md:147:- IMPLEMENTATION: Both protocol bindings consume the checked `lcg64-v1` regression corpus. Four fixed 64-bit seeds drive 2,096 deterministic cases across both envelope directions, legal and mutated frames, hostile declared lengths, arbitrary chunking/coalescing, inner HEV parsing, EOF, cancellation, and reset. Each language derives the same four stable semantic digests, so code/phase/scope/disposition or ordering drift fails the common gate without comparing implementation-specific error text.
LOGBOOK.md:154:- IMPLEMENTATION: A Python-standard-library reference path now emits and independently parses 89 canonical vectors covering both hello directions, all six message types and legal directions, all three HEV address types, every hello status and UDP error code, fixed and negotiated boundaries, malformed fields, association/session failure dispositions, and fragmented/coalesced stream plans. Limit metadata names generated schema selectors instead of copying policy values.
LOGBOOK.md:172:- IMPLEMENTATION: Swift and Go now encode the four-byte big-endian body length plus type/flags/association ID as separate header/payload write slices, and decode arbitrary partial/coalesced stream reads while retaining at most one negotiated frame plus the fixed prefix. Prefix bounds are checked before the first body allocation; generated message metadata drives direction, association-ID, fixed-payload, reserved-flag, and negotiated DNS-priority validation.
LOGBOOK.md:173:- DECISION: One `consume` call is transactional when a later coalesced frame is session-fatal: frames completed earlier in that same call are not returned or counted, while frames returned by earlier calls remain counted. This keeps the throwing Swift API and mirrored Go behavior deterministic and preserves `inputBytes = outputBytes + retainedBytes + discardedBytes` after both success and failure.
LOGBOOK.md:180:- FIX: Both incremental state machines classify a full or partial generated `RLXR` prefix already present after the accepted hello in the same callback as `duplicateHello` before publishing success, while preserving legal coalesced hello-plus-frame input.
LOGBOOK.md:186:- DECISION: Standalone exact decoders reject truncated/extended hellos, while stream state machines consume only the fixed hello prefix and hand coalesced envelope bytes to the next decoder. This preserves arbitrary SSH read boundaries without treating a valid hello-plus-frame read as an extended hello.
LOGBOOK.md:252:- MILESTONE: BUG-260720-2p4fln accepted → done; TASK-260715-35wctc unblocked. Product fixes (pre-fini stats snapshot, coalesced single boundary stop, lwIP test-lifecycle discipline) and rework-01 descriptor-gate isolation all verified.
LOGBOOK.md:273:- ROOT CAUSE / DECISION: `boundary.stop()` was a product double invocation (`requestStop()` plus `waitForReturn()`), not a bad integration expectation. A lock-coalesced stop task now invokes the boundary once and lets both lifecycle paths await the same operation; unit and real-HEV cycle tests assert one start/one stop.
LOGBOOK.md:295:- VERIFICATION: Deterministic Swift Testing now covers the synthetic 4+MTU ceiling, reverse truncation/oversize, normalized would-block spellings, both ENOBUFS directions, every persistent/fatal row, exact schema/endpoint gauges, drop-summary windows, saturation, all seven startup and seven cleanup barriers, and 100 callback-backed restart cycles. The full package passes 98 tests; 47 bridge tests also pass under ThreadSanitizer.
LOGBOOK.md:360:- IMPLEMENTATION: Child initial window/cap/adjustment policy is set through a normal pre-open channel option and observed through snapshots/events; returned credit is earned only after pipeline delivery. Client manual, per-direction protected-byte, and injected-monotonic-time rekeys share the existing KEX state machine, coalesce concurrent reasons/promises, reset generation counters on success, and observe server-initiated KEX without product reflection or a test-only API.
